def recognition_page():
    more=''.join(f'<article class="mini-tool"><h3>{e(a["title"])}</h3><p><strong>{e(a["organization"])}</strong></p><p>{e(a["description"])}</p>{link(a["url"],a["cta"])}</article>' for a in additional)
    return intro('Recognition & impact','Useful work.<br>Shared more widely.','Features, interviews, educational contributions, and research. A record of the work, with the original sources close at hand.')+f'''<section class="section" id="openai"><div class="wrap"><div class="recognition-grid full">{''.join(recognition_card(r,i==0) for i,r in enumerate(recognitions))}</div><p class="evidence-note">Explore the original publications, interviews, and educational programmes through the links above.</p>{follow_note("Follow the work as it grows.", "I share new educational contributions, practical AI ideas, and learning resources on LinkedIn.")}</div></section><section class="section light"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><h2>Further contributions & conversations.</h2></div><div class="mini-tools">{more}</div></div></section><section class="section" id="pathshala"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-intro"><div class="overline">A closer look</div><h2>Python Ki Pathshala:<br>learning in a language that feels like home.</h2></div><div class="case-grid"><div class="case-copy"><h3>The learning challenge</h3><p>A first encounter with programming can be difficult enough without an unfamiliar language getting in the way. Python Ki Pathshala brings Hindi, English, and Hinglish into the learning conversation.</p><h3>A tutor that connects ideas</h3><p>The custom GPT adapts explanations through everyday metaphors and storytelling. A cricket example can introduce a loop; a familiar situation can make an abstract idea less intimidating. Learners can ask questions, revisit explanations, and work step by step.</p><h3>Designed for understanding</h3><p>The aim is to support the learner’s thinking: connect concepts, practice with examples, and ask better questions. Educators can use the tutor alongside classroom activities and their own judgment.</p><h3>What the evidence says</h3><p>OpenAI’s June 2026 interview reports a 4.58/5 learner rating from 73 students and more than 1,000 conversations. This is reported learner feedback, rather than a controlled evaluation of learning outcomes.</p><div class="actions">{btn(GPT,'Explore Python Ki Pathshala')}{link('https://edunewsletter.openai.com/p/breaking-barriers-in-coding-education','Read the OpenAI interview')}</div></div><aside><div class="quote-panel"><p>Better access begins with meeting learners where they are.</p><small>The guiding idea behind multilingual, personalized programming support.</small></div><div style="margin-top:28px">{tutor()}</div></aside></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><h2>Impact takes more than one form.</h2></div><div class="mini-tools"><article class="mini-tool"><h3>Open learning</h3><p>CS Simplified shares computer science and AI lessons through a growing public video library.</p>{link('learning.html','Explore learning resources')}</article><article class="mini-tool"><h3>Institutional learning</h3><p>Faculty development, academic training, and professional workshops turn ideas into practical capabilities.</p>{link('talks.html','Browse documented engagements')}</article><article class="mini-tool"><h3>Research contributions</h3><p>Graph learning, network analysis, and computational research provide the foundations for applied work.</p>{link('about.html#publications','Read selected publications')}</article></div></div></section>{collab()}'''
